== About Me
I am an Assistant Professor in the Department of Mathematics and Statistics at Toulouse School of Economics (TSE), where I hold a Chaire de Professeur Junior (CPJ). \n 
My research explores the interplay between privacy, statistical learning, and economic incentives. \n 
Previously, I was a postdoctoral fellow in the [https://team.inria.fr/fairplay/ Inria FairPlay team] at CREST, ENSAE, working with [https://vianney.ai/ Vianney Perchet]. \n 
I completed my PhD in the [https://team.inria.fr/scool/ Scool team] (previously SequeL) at Inria Lille under the supervision of [https://debabrota-basu.github.io/ Debabrota Basu] and [https://philippe-preux.github.io/ Philippe Preux]. \n 
Prior to my PhD, I graduated from École Polytechnique and ENS Paris-Saclay. \n 
You can find my PhD thesis [PhD_thesis.pdf here]. The slides of my PhD presentation are also available [phd-thesis-slides/index.html here]. 


== Open Position
I am looking for a Master’s student for a research internship starting around April 2027 (4–5 months), on topics at the intersection of privacy, statistical learning, and game theory. Candidates should have a strong mathematical background. The internship could lead to a PhD under my supervision, with dedicated funding available through my CPJ. Please see the [Privacy_Incentives_Internship_TSE.pdf full internship offer] for details, and contact me directly by email if you are interested.

== Interests
My research interests include:
- Differential Privacy 
- Multi-armed Bandits
- Reinforcement Learning
- Membership Inference Attacks
- Privacy Auditing
- Prophet Inequalities
- AI Alignment


